# Face Recognition Homework

Wtire a web app that recieves a video stream from a camera. When
a face is recognized in the video, and the face is directed
at the screen and it takes up 20 percent of the image or more,
play a video on the screen. When the face is directed away from 
the screen pause the video. When the face takes less than 20
percent of the screen stop the video to be ready to play from the
beginning when a face is recognized again.
The app should be written in vanilla javascript and use yarn as a package manager.

## Requirements

Implement the following requirements using face-api.js and vanilla javascript.
- When no one is in front of the camera, show a default image
- When someone is looking at the camera, show the default image
- When someone is looking at the camera from the side, show a different image
- When the person looks back at the camera, show the default image
- When there is more than one person, show the default image and don't change it
- Detect faces better
- Run it with a network camera
- Run with an external server
